    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b22b3e2257acb2e80c45ef84130f68ab20568bc88c5acd2b7cd44cc7143d51ea",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source's reported lower-bound computation is a dependency chain: the cited Jensen implication turns one nonreal Jensen zero into a bound on Λ; the moments and quadrature construct the polynomial coefficients while separately controlling the integral tail and kernel-series truncation and empirically checking mesh stability; Sturm counting replaces enumeration of every zero; and a real-root deficit is interpretable only after the interval is made large enough to contain all real roots and the finite-precision sign pattern is stabilized. No one parent supplies this complete relation among analytic reduction, coefficient construction, algebraic decision procedure, and numerical preconditions.",
